@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    With the threading backend, starting a looping call again as soon as
+    ``wait()`` had returned could raise ``RuntimeError: A fixed interval
+    looping call can only run one function at a time``, because ``wait()``
+    returned before the finished loop's thread was released. A loop that
+    has signalled done is now treated as finished, so it can be restarted
+    straight away.
